entity.description:
Open-es is a systemic initiative that brings together SMEs, large companies, procurement divisions, banks, investors and institutions to collaborate on a common path to improve ESG performance.
A free platform for all players along the entire value chain (suppliers and customers), dedicated to sustainable business development, to make companies more competitive.

After signing-up and following a quick introduction, businesses can use Open-es to:

• MEASURE their sustainability performance and create their own ESG profile;
• SHARE data and sustainability information with customers, banks, associations and other stakeholders without replicating them;
• EVALUATE industry benchmarks and identify areas of strength and ideas for improvement;
• RECEIVE sustainability reports to respond to regulatory requirements, and business reports – including a first version of the Sustainability Report;
• COLLABORATE with the community, participating in training events focused on business needs and sharing concerns/solutions in dedicated collaboration areas.

A useful instrument for every sector – designed together with leading SMEs – to guide all companies on a path of awareness and improvement towards the most important ratings and certifications present in the Open-es development hub, an area where companies can find ESG solutions, services and information at regulatory levels useful for their own sustainability journey and Scope 3 objectives.
Openness, Collaboration and Ecosystem are the key words of Open-es, allowing everyone to join forces and achieve our sustainable development goals together.
